values ('b2c3d4e5-6f7a-4c22-9d12-2e3f4a5b6c22', 'cultural-anthropology', 'Cultural Anthropology', 'This course introduces cultural anthropology as the comparative, ethnographic study of human meaning, practice, power, and social life. Students examine culture, fieldwork, ethics, kinship, gender, economy, politics, ritual, race, language, globalization, medicine, environment, technology, theory, and applied/public anthropology. The course emphasizes cultural relativism, critical comparison, reflexive methods, ethical representation, and the public relevance of anthropological insight.');

